      ":question/worked-solution": "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(5,7).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ and $y=7$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 49 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{49}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{5}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{49}{5}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{10y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
